    "The customer mentions both recurring monthly direct-debit donations and one-off donations from multiple donors. Each donation from each donor is a separate decision unit requiring its own assessment. This representation covers only the single £95 transaction from Devon Gray on 1 March 2026."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The passages do not specify the precise monetary benefit threshold referenced in E11, so the exact limit cannot be represented as a numeric atom.",
    "The passages do not define what constitutes a valid Gift Aid declaration (e.g. required content, duration, or format), so the completeness or validity of a partial or unsigned declaration cannot be fully assessed from the supplied text alone.",
    "E03 and E06/E07 contain overlapping but slightly differently worded versions of the donor tax condition; both have been cited and treated as expressing the same requirement.",
    "The passages do not address whether a Gift Aid declaration made for an earlier gift automatically covers later gifts, so the scope of coverage of Devon's earlier declaration cannot be resolved from the supplied passages."
  ]
